in a single finding. And that's not how discovery in science works, right? If we want to make a claim that something is a truth about people in psychology, that's often what we want to do. We want to say this is a truth about people, their behaviors, their beliefs, their traits, you're not going to typically come to a definitive conclusion about all people from one study, especially very small studies. Discovery involves sort of incremental understanding of an idea and testing it in a wide range of contexts to make sure it actually applies more broadly.

